<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amago Tsunehisa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1458">1458</a>–<a href="/years/1541">1541</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amago Tsunehisa was a Japanese warlord of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sengoku-period">Sengoku period</a> who rose from deputy governor to become master of Izumo, seizing Gassan-Toda castle in 1486. He expanded Amago power across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanin-region">San'in region</a> of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a> and contested the region with the Ōuchi, making the Amago one of the great houses of the period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amago-tsunehisa.jpg" alt="Amago Tsunehisa" width="320" height="564" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E7%B4%99%E6%9C%AC%E7%9D%80%E8%89%B2%E5%B0%BC%E5%AD%90%E7%B5%8C%E4%B9%85%E5%83%8F.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
